Change(genesis='e30427e699992327267add669c3bc989f6d16525ba6f493121eec7778638e0ce', deps=('b2f77608a3145bead3e7afd92138db7d42e8614331be33039e536a6d4ad68a2c',), event=Authored(todo='typedtooling', at=datetime(2026, 11, 21, 19, 30, 17, 383196), actor='bmabsout', kind='todo', created=datetime(2026, 11, 19, 0, 0, 0), body="The merge train stops being a shell program: it is ported to a small typed Rust tool in four stages (the verdict table, publication, the gate run and its stop path, then build, land and record), each stage deleting the shell it replaces. The merge gate follows only if the train's port meets its bar: fewer guards, a faster run, and no growth in what a contributor must read.", spec=Flat(value=0.68), rationale=("A stop path's race in a shell trap could hang a train for hours, and the", 'two scripts need about two lines of test for each of their own.'), category='', waiting_on='', detail="In work on 2026-11-20: stages one and two have landed; stage three, the gate run and its stop path, is being written; stage four follows.\n\nState on 2026-11-21: stage three stopped on 2026-11-20 at its measured growth of the reading set (about ten times its projection, the ratio of the first two stages) and waited a day for an answer. Answered: the growth stands, since a train half in shell is the state the plan rules out; two holes of its stop path are closed in it (a push started and then stopped leaves no branch; the row written after the unlock is stated). The clause that the four stages must not grow the reading set has failed, so the port of the gate script does not happen. The last stage states its projected growth first, and takes over setting the context ratchet line when the train merges a change.\n\nState on 2026-11-21: stage three reviewed with two reads and sent back. Accepted: every push still passes the one check, the machine is total, the lock, the watch. To change: a lost exit status must never read as green; a piece that fails to start must end its run; the runner stops a step's leftover processes as the shell did; and the deleted guards whose property no law decides come back as laws.\n\nState on 2026-11-21: stage three landed in release 2.1.197, gated by the tool itself: the gate run and the stop path are a state machine with laws, and 674 lines of the train's shell are gone. Its first train went red on a scene of the live half that depended on the store's state (since fixed), and the tool reported it, closed its branch and let the lock go as written. Left: the last stage (build, land, record and the entry), which states its projected growth first; it takes over setting the context ratchet line at a merge, bounds the calls to the network that no signal interrupts, binds the law of a green end to the reaping loop, and holds the kill after the grace for a leader's exit.\n\nState on 2026-11-21: the last stage is paused before any code of its own landed. The plan's bar has failed on the reading set (three stages at about three tokens of Rust for each token of shell), and whether the port ends at its third stage is the owner's decision. If it ends, the one part still wanted is small and separate: the train's build sets the context ratchet line, so two accepted changes can ride one train.", source=None, subtodos=(), notes=(), note=''))